{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.neumann.edu/about/humanresources/employment#job-title-adjunct-instructor-in-math-fall-2027": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in Math (Fall 2027)",
      "description": "Job Title: Adjunct Instructor in Math (Fall 2027). Job Title: Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty JOB DESCRIPTION/DUTIES: The Jacquelyn Wilson Fegley '71 College of Nursing at Neumann University is hiring nursing clinical adjunct faculty in Nursing. Required Qualifications : Master’s degree in area of specialization and recent clinical experience required. Teaching experience preferred. Must be eligible for RN licensure in Pennsylvania and Delaware, and meet background study requirements according to institutional regulations, and Pennsylvania and Delaware statutes. Candidates must possess an appreciation for, congruence with, and commitment to the Franciscan mission of the University. For full consideration, applications must include the following materials: An application letter. A current curriculum vitae. Documentation of effective teaching. Names, phone numbers, and email address of at least three references. References will be contracted for all finalist candidates. Review of applications will begin immediately. Apply Now EOE M/F/D/V"
    },
    "https://www.neumann.edu/about/humanresources/employment#job-title-nursing-clinical-adjunct-faculty": {
      "title": "Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Job Title: Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty. Job Title: Adjunct Instructor in Biology JOB DESCRIPTION/DUTIES: The Neumann University School of Nursing & Health Sciences is seeking per course faculty adjuncts in Biology for our adjunct pool. Duties & Responsibilities: We are especially interested in colleagues who can teach in-person sections of Anatomy and Physiology for Nursing and Health Science majors, Biochemical Lab Techniques and Cellular and Molecular Biology lecture and lab for Biology majors. Availability throughout the morning and afternoon hours. All other professionals with specializations in other areas of Biology (e.g., Microbiology for Nursing Majors, Clinical Laboratory Sciences courses, etc.) are also invited to apply for our adjunct pool. Required Qualifications : A completed master’s degree or a terminal degree from a regionally accredited institution of higher education in the field for which they are applying to teach. Candidates must possess an appreciation for, congruence with, and commitment to the Franciscan mission of the University that values diversity, equity, and inclusion. For full consideration, applications must include the following materials: An application letter. A current curriculum vitae or resume. Contact information for three (3) references (names, titles, employers, phone numbers, and email addresses). Documentation of effective teaching. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Apply Now EOE M/F/D/V"
    },
    "https://www.neumann.edu/about/humanresources/employment#job-title-adjunct-instructor-in-biology": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in Biology",
      "description": "Job Title: Adjunct Instructor in Biology. Job Title: Adjunct Instructor in Chemistry JOB DESCRIPTION/DUTIES: The Neumann University School of Nursing & Health Sciences is seeking per course faculty adjuncts in Chemistry for our adjunct pool. Duties & Responsibilities: We are especially interested in colleagues who can teach in-person or hybrid sections of Chemistry lectures and in-person labs. Availability throughout the morning and afternoon hours. All other professionals with specializations in other areas of Chemistry (e.g., Organic Chemistry Labs, Biochemistry Lab, Clinical Biochemistry Lab, etc.) are also invited to apply for our adjunct pool. Required Qualifications : A completed master’s degree or a terminal degree from a regionally accredited institution of higher education in the field for which they are applying to teach. Candidates must possess an appreciation for, congruence with, and commitment to the Franciscan mission of the University that values diversity, equity, and inclusion. For full consideration, applications must include the following materials: An application letter. A current curriculum vitae or resume. Contact information for three (3) references (names, titles, employers, phone numbers, and email addresses). Documentation of effective teaching. Apply Now EOE M/F/D/V"
    },
    "https://www.neumann.edu/about/humanresources/employment#job-title-adjunct-instructor-in-chemistry": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in Chemistry",
      "description": "Job Title: Adjunct Instructor in Chemistry. Job Title: Adjunct Instructor in English JOB DESCRIPTION/DUTIES: The Neumann University School of Social Sciences, Humanities & Education invites applications for per course faculty adjuncts in first-year writing. Duties & Responsibilities: We are only interested in colleagues who can teach in-person sections on our Aston, PA campus at this time. Availability throughout the morning and afternoon. Required Qualifications : A completed master’s degree or a terminal degree from a regionally accredited institution of higher education in the field of English or a related discipline. Documented experience working with writers from diverse backgrounds is preferred. Candidates must possess an appreciation for, congruence with, and commitment to the Franciscan mission of the University that values diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging. For full consideration, applications must include the following materials: A letter of interest A current curriculum vitae Contact information for three (3) references (names, titles, employers, phone numbers, and email addresses) Documentation of effective teaching. Review of applications will begin immediately. Apply Now EOE M/F/D/V"
    },
    "https://www.neumann.edu/about/humanresources/employment#job-title-assistant-professor-business-administration-entrepreneurship": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Business Administration & Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Job Title: Assistant Professor – Business Administration & Entrepreneurship. Job Title: Adjunct Instructor in Math (Fall 2027) JOB DESCRIPTION/DUTIES: The School of Business at Neumann University invites applications for Adjunct Instructors of Mathematics to teach undergraduate mathematics courses during the Fall 2027 semester. (Note that these are math classes, not business math classes.) We seek student-centered educators who are committed to academic excellence, engaged learning, and supporting student success in a diverse learning environment. Courses may include, college algebra and/or introductory statistics, or other mathematics courses based on departmental needs. Preference will be given to candidates who are available to teach in person on the Neumann University campus Duties & Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate mathematics courses. Prepare and deliver engaging course content aligned with approved learning outcomes. Maintain regular communication with students and provide timely feedback on assignments and assessments. Be available to students as needed. Submit attendance, grades, and other required reports by established deadlines. Utilize the University's learning management system (CANVAS) and, if needed, instructional technologies. Support the mission and values of Neumann University Required Qualifications : A degree in mathematics or a closely related field and a graduate degree from an accredited institution. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate mathematics courses. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Commitment to student success and inclusive teaching practices. Candidates must possess an appreciation for, congruence with, and commitment to the Franciscan mission of the University. Preferred Qualifications : Previous college-level teaching experience. Experience teaching in both traditional and technology-enhanced learning environments. Availability to teach in-person courses. Experience working with diverse student populations. For full consideration, applications must include the following materials: A cover letter. A current curriculum vitae or resume. Unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire). Names, phone numbers, and email address of at least three references. References will be contracted for all finalist candidates. About Neumann University Neumann University is a private Catholic institution rooted in the Franciscan tradition, committed to academic excellence, respect for the dignity of all persons, and preparing students to transform the world through service and leadership. Neumann University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals who will contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Apply Now EOE M/F/D/V"
    },
    "https://www.neumann.edu/about/humanresources/employment#job-title-assistant-associate-professor-clinical-psychology": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor – Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor – Clinical Psychology. Job Title: Assistant Professor – Business Administration & Entrepreneurship JOB DESCRIPTION/DUTIES: The School of Business at Neumann University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Business Administration and Entrepreneurship, beginning in August 2027. We seek a dynamic, innovative, and student-centered educator who is passionate about entrepreneurship, experiential learning, and preparing students to become creative problem-solvers and responsible business leaders. In addition to teaching, we are particularly interested in a candidate who has the vision, leadership, and entrepreneurial experience to serve as coordinator of the Center for Entrepreneurship. The ideal candidate will help advance entrepreneurship across the University, create opportunities for student-run ventures, and cultivate an entrepreneurial mindset among students from all academic disciplines. This position offers an opportunity to help shape the future of entrepreneurship at Neumann University by connecting academic learning with real-world experiences, fostering interdisciplinary collaboration, and building meaningful relationships with the regional business community. Salary and rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Duties & Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to: Teach undergraduate courses in Business Administration and Entrepreneurship, with the flexibility to teach courses in management, finance, human resources, international business, or related business disciplines based on expertise and program needs. Contribute to curriculum development, innovative teaching practices, and experiential learning opportunities within the School of Business. Integrate emerging business trends, technology, and artificial intelligence into teaching and learning, where appropriate. Mentor and advise students in their academic, professional, and entrepreneurial development. Maintain an active commitment to scholarship, research, professional development, University service, and community engagement. Teach the standard faculty load of 12 credits per academic semester, with assignments determined by academic and institutional needs. Center for Entrepreneurship Leadership : Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate the qualifications and interest to assume a leadership role as coordinator of the Center for Entrepreneurship. Responsibilities associated with this role may include: Promoting and integrating entrepreneurship across the University, creating opportunities for students and faculty from all academic disciplines to engage in entrepreneurial learning and innovation. Developing and supporting student-run ventures that provide hands-on opportunities for students to launch, manage, and grow businesses. Collaborating with faculty across academic schools to incorporate entrepreneurial thinking, innovation, and problem-solving into courses and interdisciplinary initiatives. Organizing entrepreneurship competitions, workshops, mentoring programs, and other activities that encourage students to transform ideas into viable ventures. Building relationships with entrepreneurs, alumni, business leaders, and community organizations to expand mentorship, internship, and experiential learning opportunities. Identifying potential external funding, sponsorships, and partnerships to support the Center’s activities and long-term sustainability. The Center’s leadership responsibilities and any associated teaching-load adjustments will be determined based on institutional priorities and available resources. Required Qualifications : A master’s degree in Business Administration, Entrepreneurship, Management, or a closely related business discipline. A Ph.D., DBA, or other relevant terminal degree is preferred. Demonstrated knowledge of business administration and entrepreneurship, with the ability to teach undergraduate courses in both areas. University-level teaching experience or demonstrated potential for excellence in undergraduate instruction. Strong communication, interpersonal, leadership, and collaborative skills. A commitment to student success, innovative teaching, and experiential learning. An appreciation for, congruence with, and commitment to the Catholic Franciscan mission of Neumann University. Preferred Qualifications : Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate several of the following qualifications: A Ph.D. or DBA in Business Administration, Entrepreneurship, Management, or a closely related discipline. Professional experience as an entrepreneur, business owner, consultant, or business development leader. Experience establishing, leading, or expanding an entrepreneurship center, academic entrepreneurship program, or similar initiative. Demonstrated success in developing, launching, or mentoring student-run businesses and entrepreneurial ventures. Experience integrating entrepreneurship across multiple academic disciplines and fostering interdisciplinary collaboration. Experience developing relationships with entrepreneurs, alumni, industry partners, and community organizations. Experience securing external funding, sponsorships, or other resources to support entrepreneurship initiatives. Demonstrated ability to teach across multiple business disciplines. Experience incorporating artificial intelligence, emerging technologies, and innovative teaching approaches into business education. Experience teaching online or hybrid courses. A record of scholarship, applied research, or professional engagement in business administration or entrepreneurship. degree Faculty Protocol : Candidates should be aware that Neumann University does not have a system of tenure but instead offers faculty a policy-governed system of promotion and increasingly extended contracts with faculty seniority. Application Requirements: For full consideration, applications must include the following materials: A letter of interest addressing the candidate’s qualifications, teaching experience, expertise in Business Administration and Entrepreneurship, and appreciation for and commitment to the Catholic Franciscan mission of the University. Candidates interested in leading the Center for Entrepreneurship are encouraged to describe their vision for promoting entrepreneurship across campus and developing student-run ventures. A current curriculum vitae or resume. If applicable, teaching evaluations, sample syllabi, and/or other evidence of demonstrated excellence in undergraduate instruction. Copies of graduate and undergraduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be required at the time of hire. Contact information for three professional references. Letters of recommendation are not required during the initial review process but will be requested from finalists. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Apply Now EOE M/F/D/V"
    },
    "https://www.neumann.edu/about/humanresources/employment#job-title-instructor-assistant-professor-biology": {
      "title": "Instructor/Assistant Professor – Biology",
      "description": "Job Title: Instructor/Assistant Professor – Biology. Job Title: Adjunct Instructor in Biology JOB DESCRIPTION/DUTIES: The Neumann University School of Nursing & Health Sciences is seeking per course faculty adjuncts in Biology for our adjunct pool. Duties & Responsibilities: We are especially interested in colleagues who can teach in-person sections of Anatomy and Physiology for Nursing and Health Science majors, Biochemical Lab Techniques and Cellular and Molecular Biology lecture and lab for Biology majors. Availability throughout the morning and afternoon hours. All other professionals with specializations in other areas of Biology (e.g., Microbiology for Nursing Majors, Clinical Laboratory Sciences courses, etc.) are also invited to apply for our adjunct pool. Required Qualifications : A completed master’s degree or a terminal degree from a regionally accredited institution of higher education in the field for which they are applying to teach. Candidates must possess an appreciation for, congruence with, and commitment to the Franciscan mission of the University that values diversity, equity, and inclusion. For full consideration, applications must include the following materials: An application letter. A current curriculum vitae or resume. Contact information for three (3) references (names, titles, employers, phone numbers, and email addresses). Documentation of effective teaching. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Apply Now EOE M/F/D/V"
